namic body to node A in that case. The godot behavior causes limits to behave in a strange unintuitive way. You can flip Jolt to behave as godot by setting the following setting:\n\n\nJolt and GodotPhysics have the same malfunction :(","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848776031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2849374890","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105931#issuecomment-2849374890","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105931","id":2849374890,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6p1gKq","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-04T19:17:58Z","updated_at":"2025-05-04T19:17:58Z","body":"The MRP project you provided looks fine to me with Jolt and godot 4.4.1:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c9aff53-53be-4a2f-b68c-7140c5011b59","author_association":"CONTRIB